 <<  1 : DESCRIPTION  >>
 
   KST32B(File=KST32B.TXT) is KST('Kanji'-StrokeTable:FontDefine) of
  Model of JIS(JapanIndustrialStandard) defined Chinese and other
  character.
 
   This version include,
   a: ASCII (8bit) char :                             0020--007E,
   b: Japanse-Kana 8bit char :                        00A1--00DF,
   c: ISO 8859-15 8bit char(except 0xAD) :           (00A0--00FF),
      BUT, it(=c) is Mapped to                        1A20--1A7F,
   d: JIS Level-1 Non-'Kanji' 16bit char :            2121--2E34,
   e: JIS Level-1 'Kanji' set(about 3000ch) :         3021--4F7E,
   f: JIS Level-2 'Kanji' char :                      5021--7426.
 
   SPECIFICATION of this KST(CSF/1-format) is described in Header-
  Comment of KST file(Line 1 to 22,etc.); That is, CSF/1-format is pure
  Plain-Text (0x20--7E,A1--DF) format!
   Format name CSF/1 mean CompactStrokeFontFormat/ver1; It's merit is
  very compact in byte-size(160KB: Except JIS Level-2).  But not best
  quality.
   KST32B font is based on JIS/C6226 and JIS/X0208. But not strictly.

   
 
 
