 <<  3 : NOTICE  >>
 
  (3.1)  Relation TOOL : 
     Perhaps, this font cannot use generally!  Because, FontFormat
    (=CSF/1) is not general type.
     KST-Tool(KST-Viewer,print,conversion,update) is available on 
    Vector-Web-site. Name is 'KSTool'. It is mainly for Unix(Linux) &
    X-Window.  But, minimum(=simplest) viewer KSTVW1 for MS-Windows
    (95,98,98se,Me,2000,Xp,etc.) and NEC/PC-9801 is included.
 
  (3.2)  Bitmap Expand Size : 
     In case of expand to Bitmap(= Draw to Pixmap), this KST asuume
    12--150 pixel height.  Most suitable size is 30x32(=XY) pixel.
     Line width assume 1.1--1.9, at 30x32pixel case.  But not so wrong,
    if width is more fat.  Cap-form(type) of draw line is recomend to
    circle type.
 
  (3.3)  Version_Up History : 
   (3.3.1) KST32A  : 1999/10
     1st Open(Vector-Web-site); JIS Level-1 char, created on 1992/06
    by about 2 mounth.
   (3.3.2) KST32B ver 1.0 : 2001/03
     Add small part of JIS Level-2 char, also add 8bit-ASCII, 8bit-
    Japanese-Kana.   Change expression of part of 'Kanji' char, from
    JIS/C6226 to X0208. etc.
   (3.3.3) KST32B ver 2.0 : 2004/01
     Add almost part(80%) of JIS Level-2 'Kanji', and Add ISO 8859-15
    char.  Look again JIS Level-1 'Kanji' expression.  Add 16bit Euro
    currency sign, at 0x2921(temporary). etc.
   (3.3.4) KST32B ver 3.0 : 2017/07
     Finally completed JIS Level-2 'Kanji' input!
 
  (3.4)  Address space of 8bit char : 
     CSF/1 have 30x32 address space. It is used to 16bit(wide) char.
     Case of 8bit char, KST32B use it's left-half space(15x32).
 
  (3.5) ISO88599 Address offset :
     Code area of ISO8859 and JIS-Kana is overlapping. So, according 
    to store both font in single file, former code is offset +0x1980.
     Original 0xA1 to FF is mapped to 0x1A21 to 1A7F.

  (3.6)  0x5C as Japanese Yen-sign extension :
     This font defined 0x5C code as Back Slash(=ASCII). If case of 
    treated Yen-sign, then copy ISO8859 Yen-sign(code 0xA5: internal  
    code 1A25 in this KST).
   (3.6.1) Comment out('*') 005C ... line.
   (3.6.2) Copy 1A25 ... line and rewrite 1A25 to 005C.
 
 
